T* (      Harry Potter spends a miserable summer with the Dursleys, wishing to escape his unkind relatives and connect) Tj
T* (with his magical world. Despite having his magic belongings locked away, he secretly studies his homework. After) Tj
T* (a phone call from Ron angers Uncle Vernon, Harry feels isolated. On his birthday, he hopes for his owl, Hedwig, to) Tj
T* (return, and three owls arrive with gifts and messages from friends, bringing joy to his otherwise lonely day. He) Tj
T* (receives thoughtful presents, including a Pocket Sneakoscope and a Broomstick Servicing Kit, and finds a lively) Tj
T* (book, The Monster Book of Monsters. A letter from Hogwarts reveals details about the new school year,) Tj
T* (highlighting his desire to have his Hogsmeade permission slip signed by Uncle Vernon. The chapter closes with) Tj
T* (Harry feeling a mix of joy and anxiety, longing for acceptance and adventure in the wizarding world.) Tj
